  "summary": "Extracts arbitrary-parent block template reconstruction into a shared RebuildBlockForParent test helper used by BuildChain and MinerTestingSetup::Block. The helper updates the header hash and timestamp, recalculates the proof-of-work target and block subsidy from the target parent, appends a dummy OP_0 to satisfy minimum coinbase script length on low heights, and asserts coinbase-only templates.",
  "problem": "Test utilities creating fork blocks by repointing active-tip templates could retain the active tip's work target or subsidy, and produced coinbase scripts below the minimum length requirement at heights 1 through 16. Existing test callers either avoided these boundary conditions or worked around them locally, but new tests constructing forks could produce invalid blocks.",
